\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Capability profile across controlled training conditions.} Cells report raw percentages on the common covered set. Color encodes the within-row change from Base on a shared $\pm 20$-percentage-point scale: blue is higher, orange is lower, and saturation indicates magnitude. Candidate alignment produces a broad gain in selection and continuation recall, whereas answer-only supervision does not. The final \textsc  {EGO}{} model further strengthens retention and continuation recovery, without improving every axis. The two evidence-conditioned rows are descriptive associations, not interventions.\relax }}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
