\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A state-bearing belief enables correction when an action-copying belief does not.} The four evaluated policies receive the same observation, completed-action history, shuffled candidate set, and prompt. Generated traces are reproduced verbatim, with \ldots  {} marking omitted text. To avoid anecdotal selection, we apply a fixed criterion to the common covered set: all four traces must be valid, GT-only must copy its chosen action into the belief field and answer incorrectly, and \textsc  {EGO}{} must answer correctly. This criterion identifies \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$31$} of \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$915$} points; the example shown is one of the \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$18$} for which Cand.-CE is also incorrect. \underline  {Underlined} spans explicitly reference prior actions under the same rule used for the mention-rate analysis, whereas \textbf  {bold} spans express the model's current task state.\relax }}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
